error[type.mismatch]: `A` and `B` are two types — a named type never mixes with another
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:3:33]
3 │ fn f(a: A, b: B) -> bool { a == b }
  ·                                 ┬
  ·                                 ╰── this is `B`
──╯
help: a named type is its own type — `Name(value)` crosses in and `.of` reads its shape out
